  "language": "en",
  "text": "Raise your prices a little on your septic services. Your customers won't even feel it, but your margin will. I met with a client today whose investors gave them a list of changes. One of them was raising prices. They walked me through the list and I told them honestly they were good changes, especially the price increase. A small increase barely registers with the company. Over a year it becomes a cushion that carries you through the surprises. We all know what happens. Margin isn't greed. It's how you get through the month the truck breaks down. If you've been putting off price increase, you're not crazy for being nervous, but it's probably the first thing I look at.",
